2025-05-01 03:24:19 - Thread-1391 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

salesperson  
• businessentityid – primary key to identify each salesperson (will be joined to SalesPersonQuotaHistory and salesorderheader.salespersonid).  

salesorderheader  
• salespersonid ­– foreign key to salesperson.businessentityid.  
• orderdate – will be converted to year (strftime('%Y', orderdate)).  
• totaldue – represents the value of each order; will be summed to obtain a salesperson’s annual sales.  
• (Optional) status / onlineorderflag – could be used to exclude cancelled orders etc. If necessary: WHERE status NOT IN (‘6’,‘7’)  --‑ only if the data set shows cancelled orders.  

SalesPersonQuotaHistory  
• businessentityid – foreign key to salesperson.businessentityid.  
• quotadate – will be converted to year (strftime('%Y', quotadate)).  
• salesquota – the quota amount to aggregate per year.  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
• JOIN salesorderheader ON salesperson.businessentityid = salesorderheader.salespersonid  
• JOIN SalesPersonQuotaHistory ON salesperson.businessentityid = SalesPersonQuotaHistory.businessentityid  
• GROUP BY salesperson.businessentityid, strftime('%Y', …)  
• HAVING SUM(totaldue) IS NOT NULL AND SUM(salesquota) IS NOT NULL  --‑ to keep only years where both exist.  

Exploratory / step‑by‑step queries  
Each query is limited to 20 rows and shows progressively more complex slices of the data, finishing with the full answer.

```sql
-- 1. List distinct salespeople that ever appear on an order
SELECT DISTINCT salespersonid
FROM salesorderheader
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List distinct salespeople that have quotas
SELECT DISTINCT businessentityid
FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Peek at the quota dates to understand their format
SELECT DISTINCT quotadate
FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
ORDER BY quotadate
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Extract the year component of quota dates
SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y', quotadate) AS quota_year
FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
ORDER BY quota_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Extract the year component of order dates
SELECT DISTINCT strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS order_year
FROM salesorderheader
ORDER BY order_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Annual total sales (totaldue) per salesperson (raw values)
SELECT salespersonid,
       strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS order_year,
       SUM(totaldue) AS annual_sales
FROM salesorderheader
GROUP BY salespersonid, order_year
ORDER BY salespersonid, order_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Annual quota per salesperson (raw values)
SELECT businessentityid,
       strftime('%Y', quotadate) AS quota_year,
       SUM(salesquota) AS annual_quota
FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
GROUP BY businessentityid, quota_year
ORDER BY businessentityid, quota_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Combine sales and quota for years where both exist
SELECT s.businessentityid,
       s.year,
       s.annual_sales,
       q.annual_quota
FROM (
        SELECT salespersonid AS businessentityid,
               strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS year,
               SUM(totaldue) AS annual_sales
        FROM salesorderheader
        GROUP BY salespersonid, year
     ) AS s
JOIN (
        SELECT businessentityid,
               strftime('%Y', quotadate) AS year,
               SUM(salesquota) AS annual_quota
        FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
        GROUP BY businessentityid, year
     ) AS q
  ON s.businessentityid = q.businessentityid
 AND s.year = q.year
ORDER BY s.businessentityid, s.year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Add the difference between sales and quota
SELECT s.businessentityid,
       s.year,
       s.annual_sales,
       q.annual_quota,
       (s.annual_sales - q.annual_quota) AS diff_sales_vs_quota
FROM (
        SELECT salespersonid AS businessentityid,
               strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS year,
               SUM(totaldue) AS annual_sales
        FROM salesorderheader
        GROUP BY salespersonid, year
     ) AS s
JOIN (
        SELECT businessentityid,
               strftime('%Y', quotadate) AS year,
               SUM(salesquota) AS annual_quota
        FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
        GROUP BY businessentityid, year
     ) AS q
  ON s.businessentityid = q.businessentityid
 AND s.year = q.year
ORDER BY s.businessentityid, s.year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer – show every salesperson / year, sales, quota, and difference
SELECT s.businessentityid   AS salesperson_id,
       s.year               AS sales_year,
       s.annual_sales       AS total_sales,
       q.annual_quota       AS total_quota,
       (s.annual_sales - q.annual_quota) AS difference_sales_minus_quota
FROM (
        SELECT salespersonid AS businessentityid,
               strftime('%Y', orderdate) AS year,
               SUM(totaldue) AS annual_sales
        FROM salesorderheader
        GROUP BY salespersonid, year
     ) AS s
LEFT JOIN (
        SELECT businessentityid,
               strftime('%Y', quotadate) AS year,
               SUM(salesquota) AS annual_quota
        FROM SalesPersonQuotaHistory
        GROUP BY businessentityid, year
     ) AS q
  ON s.businessentityid = q.businessentityid
 AND s.year = q.year
ORDER BY salesperson_id, sales_year
LIMIT 20;
```

The tenth query furnishes, for every salesperson and year in which they have orders, the summed Total Sales, summed Quota, and the difference (positive means they exceeded quota, negative means they fell short).
